{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T02:01:13.150Z","author":"codex-github230-1111","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fb26b8f462e36ea161357e8c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T02:01:13.150Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-12T02:01:13.150Z","author":"codex-github230-1111","text":"Round 7 is the final fix round for #233. This single follow-up consolidates additional review observations, as requested by the orchestrator; it does not assert that every observation reproduces after the round-7 changes. Validate each against the final head, deduplicate covered cases, and retain real SDK must-refuse/must-allow tests plus behavioral revert evidence for any fix.\n\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBR](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876674): Report import conflicts on the workflow path that produces no tracker diff.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBZ](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876686): Validate ambiguous legacy number-only ownership before closeout.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBc](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876691): Recover exclusive leases safely when publication succeeds but directory flush fails.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBe](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876695): Require an actual matching reference tag before planning tag detachment.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBi](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876701): Reconcile contradictory external_ref claims at the import write boundary.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBo](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876710): Check partial legacy link markers against an existing repository field.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBu](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876718): Avoid retaining an ownership-refused plan when no SDK journal exists.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876728): Scope retained recovery plans to selected refresh IDs without dropping fresh updates.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876736): Handle contradictory identities in blocker self-exclusion; dependency indexing is addressed in round 7.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB_](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876746): Use canonical lowercase reference tags in the citation-adoption fixture.\n\nExplicit identity-conflict isolation in closeout and real-tracker dry-run fixtures are already addressed by round 7. Existing curated-reopen, Projects and search follow-ups keep their separate scope. Do not delete append-only tracker evidence or reply to/resolve review threads while implementing this follow-up.\n\nPM: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-github-reference-identity-followup.toon"}]}],"before_hash":"7e6432ed1aecc1058f43b07f0b0c2b1d2130c950b4cfa13548f50f3a7806c249","after_hash":"414b866a48b6e0a00935cfc436669467e90e54afb2becf593df2b8ef382cd12e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ff2dfa79bcce3957ee3fcac60156023395e93d88e00b29e7dc0770ffafcc66f9"}
